MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The magnets with screw holes fit my recent interest in magnetic hooks and fasteners because they give me another practical way to mount and hang things.",
    "The digital caliper relates to my screw and washer purchases because it could help check dimensions, although I would only choose it when I actually need to measure something."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The printer filaments do not serve the fastening or hanging needs reflected in my recent purchases; buying hardware does not mean I have a printing project.",
    "The feeler gauge and wire connectors require specific gap-measuring or wiring tasks that I have not shown a need for. Being useful workshop supplies is not enough for me to choose them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical hardware seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any workshop or making supply.",
    "The repeated filament suggestions assume a printing need without evidence that I use a 3D printer. Different colors and materials do not make them more relevant to my current tasks."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases repeatedly involve fastening, magnetic attachment, and hanging; those specific uses matter more to me than a broad connection to tools.",
    "I rarely choose something just because it might be useful someday. A clear immediate use matters, which is why the mounting magnets appeal more than the caliper."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my hardware interests but mostly missed the specific fastening and magnetic mounting uses that would make me choose something now."
}
